[Session 4 — 2026-05-30]
  AI sidebar module — WebView2 + TypeScript (inspired by cc-haha / Warp)

  Architecture (final):
    MainWindow root Grid uses a 2-column layout: Column 0 terminal +
      Column 1 AiSidebar.
    AiSidebar = WebView2 container -> loads webui/ai-sidebar.html
      (self-contained TS app).
    TS handles independently: SSE streaming requests, chat UI rendering,
      conversation state management.
    C# only handles: API config persistence, panel show/hide, C#<->TS bridge.
    Tab key toggles the sidebar (420px / 0px).

  C#<->TS communication protocol:
    C# -> TS: CoreWebView2.ExecuteScriptAsync("window.setConfig({...})")
    C# -> TS: ExecuteScriptAsync("window.sendPrompt('...')")
    TS -> C#: chrome.webview.postMessage({ type: 'close' })

