[Session 3 — 2026-05-17]
  Fixed frontend-backend connection — 4 key fixes:

  1) Path resolution: GetPythonScriptPath() now searches upward recursively
     for python/launcher.py (up to 6 levels). Fixes the script-not-found
     issue when the -r win-x64 build output path is too deep.

  2) Startup handshake: launcher.py sends a __READY__ signal on startup; the
     C# side waits for the handshake to complete (5s timeout). Added a
     KernelReady property that accurately reflects kernel state, replacing
     the blind 200ms wait.

  3) Double-send bug fix: forwarded commands (x++/logo/sandbox/edit/translate/
     qrcode) no longer call SendCommand directly in Exec(); they uniformly
     return the "__FORWARD__" marker, and TryForward() sends them once.
     Old code: Exec sent once + TryForward sent again = every command ran twice.

  4) Better error messages: when the kernel is offline, TryForward shows
     "Python kernel offline" instead of "Unknown command". For unknown
     commands, Execute shows the C# suggestion first, then forwards to Python
     (the Python kernel has its own fuzzy matching).

  kernel/__init__.py: ensures Python package import compatibility.
  Git init: .gitignore + initial commit (36 files, 4229 lines) + fix commit
     (3 files, +41/-20).

